        "answer": "Yes. As a German tax resident, you are subject to German income tax on worldwide income, including Turkish rental income and capital gains from Turkish property sales. The German-Turkish Double Taxation Agreement (DTA, 2011) allocates primary taxation rights for immovable property income to Turkey; Germany then credits the Turkish tax paid against the German tax liability (credit method). German taxation of gains from property held for more than 10 years (§ 23 EStG) generally does not apply after that holding period expires."
