        "question": "Can my German-citizen children (who never had Turkish citizenship) inherit my Turkish property?",
        "answer": "Yes, as regular foreign nationals. Children who were never Turkish citizens inherit as 'foreigners' (yabancı) under Turkish law. For most property types this is unproblematic — the land registry transfer is possible, though documentation requirements are more demanding. Military exclusion zones and certain strategic areas cannot be transferred to foreign nationals; in such cases the property must be liquidated and the proceeds distributed. Early estate planning — including considering lifetime transfer — is particularly advisable in these mixed-nationality situations."
