                "question": "How is Muris Muvazaası different from a forced-heirship claim (tenkis)?",
                "answer": "Tenkis (forced-heirship reduction) applies when a valid transfer exceeds the deceased's disposable portion and reduces a protected heir's share. Only forced heirs can bring it, and the court only claws back the excess amount. Muris Muvazaası applies when the transfer itself is fake — void from the start. All heirs can bring it, and if successful, the entire transfer is cancelled. If you can prove a sham, Muris Muvazaası is almost always the stronger legal route."
